Learning Commons Knowledge Graph
  Academic standards, their learning components and the standards before them, in the example
  course package examples/fractions-practice.json (its activity's standard, 5.NF.A.1) and in
  any teaching settings that keep a standard as it was chosen. Each standard carries its own
  attribution statements in source.attribution, and a package lists them in "attribution".
  Source: https://learningcommons.org
  Attribution, as the example carries it:
    Knowledge Graph is provided by Learning Commons under the CC BY-4.0 license. Common Core
    Mathematics standards provided by Common Good Learning Tools available at
    https://corestandards.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Math_Standards1.pdf.
    Knowledge Graph is provided by Learning Commons under the CC BY-4.0 license. Learning Commons
    received learning components under CC BY-4.0 from Achievement Network.
    Knowledge Graph is provided by Learning Commons under the CC BY-4.0 license. Learning Commons
    received learning progressions under CC0 from Student Achievement Partners.

Carnegie Skills Progressions (durable skills)
  Collaboration, communication and critical thinking, with their subskills, indicators and four
  levels, from a Learning Commons Knowledge Graph release: VIABLE's copy, src/utils/skillsData.js
  (lib/utils/skillsData.js in an export), exported by the kit as SKILLS, and the skill kept in
  examples/seminar-discussion.json and schemas/examples/teaching.example.json.
  Author: Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching.
  Attribution:
    Knowledge Graph is provided by Learning Commons under the CC BY-4.0 license, available at
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0. Learning Commons received the Carnegie Skills
    Progressions curriculum under CC BY-4.0 from Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of
    Teaching.

Eedi Misconceptions Graph
  Misconceptions in mathematics and the constructs they hinder, from a Learning Commons Knowledge
  Graph release: VIABLE's copy, src/utils/misconceptionsData.js, and its source and attribution in
  src/utils/misconceptionsSource.js (lib/utils/misconceptionsSource.js in an export, which the
  teaching layer imports), and any misconceptions a teacher chose and teaching settings keep, each
  with its own attribution in source.attribution.
  Author: Eedi Ltd.
  Attribution:
